  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1: A nice afternoon today, but increasing chance \nfor widespread moderate to perhaps heavy rain late Saturday into\nearly Sunday. \n\nSurface high pressure will drift across Upstate New York before \nmoving off the Southern New England Coast tonight. A\nsoutheasterly to southerly flow will develop late tonight into\nSaturday and low level moisture lurking just south of the \nMason/Dixon line will push steadily NE across the state on \nSaturday. \n\nA notable axis of streamline convergence shifting gradually \neast across Central PA late Sat afternoon/Sat night will provide\nincreasing llvl theta-E advection and numerous showers with  \nseveral tenths of an inch of rainfall likely across at least the\nSE half to two thirds of the CWA by early Sunday. \n\nA few PM TSRA are possible Saturday and/or Sunday afternoons, \nespecially over the western mtns where MU CAPE will climb above\n1000 j/kg with pocket of 0-1 KM EHI in the 1-1.5 m2/s2 range. \n\nThe timing of the thickening cloud cover late tonight/early Sat\nmorning will allow for moderate radiational cooling of the\nground tonight with the llvl inversion being difficult to break\nfor the first half of Saturday across our Central and NE zones.\nSo, Max Temps should turn out to be a few to several deg F \nlower than today's\n\nA more-active (wetter) pattern is in store for Mon- Tues. But, \nthe flat upper ridge over the southern half of the CONUS will \nmake it difficult for deep moisture to make it into PA ahead of \nany shots of atmos forcing. The week could end dry as the upper \nridge pumps up over the central CONUS.",
